<td id="S5.T1.2.17.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.2.17.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1.33</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.17.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.2.17.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1.32</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.17.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.2.17.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">26</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.2.17.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.2.17.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">35</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets and evaluation.</span>
We evaluate CAPS on nine public TSAD datasets spanning diverse
domains and anomaly characteristics: IOPS, MGAB, NAB, Power, SED,
UCR, NEK, TODS, and YAHOO.
Performance is reported using Affiliation-F,
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{F1}_{\mathrm{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F1</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{F1}_{\mathrm{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Standard-F1, and VUS-PR, covering
complementary event-level, point-wise, and range-aware
evaluation perspectives.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span>
We compare CAPS with classical methods
LOF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> and IForest <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>,
and deep models OmniAnomaly <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>,
USAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, TranAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>,
Anomaly Transformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>,
TimesNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, and FITS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>.
TCN-based references include TCN-AE, TCN-Forecast,
TCN-Injection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, and TCN-Supervised.
Appendix <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Detailed Per-Dataset Results ‣ Appendix C Experimental Setup and Detailed Results ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> additionally reports
CAPS(Diagnosis), which uses limited known anomalies only for expert
selection, without using them as detector-training labels.
Baseline descriptions and experimental protocols are provided in
Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Setup and Detailed Results ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation details.</span>
Unless otherwise specified, CAPS uses the TCN-based encoder–decoder
and independent lightweight TCN detector described in
Sec. <a href="#S4" title="4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, with sequence length 256 and
structure/anomaly latent dimensions of 128/48.
We use <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3</annotation></semantics></math> coarse semantic modes organized by simulated point,
periodic, and trend anomaly families.
Alternative mode constructions and different choices of <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>
are examined in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Extended Experiments and Analyses ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.
Implementation details are provided in
Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Setup and Detailed Results ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablations and Controlled Comparisons.</span>

Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes four comparisons using the
same TCN detector and evaluation protocol:
<em id="S5.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(1) Shuffled residuals</em> applies each generated residual to a
different target reference, shuffling its anomaly support together
with it while preserving the generator and number of generated
counterparts;
<em id="S5.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(2) Without residual parameterization</em> replaces residual-form
construction with direct anomalous-sequence generation while retaining
background-preservation supervision outside the intended anomaly
support;
<em id="S5.SS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(3) Direct source-residual injection</em> adds the observation-level
differences of the same simulated normal–anomalous pairs directly
to target references, jointly bypassing semantic learning and
target-conditioned realization;
<em id="S5.SS1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(4) Without counterfactual loss</em> removes
<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 Structured Disentanglement for Transferable Anomaly Semantics ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> while retaining
<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>dis</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}</annotation></semantics></math>, examining the contribution of
within-pair counterfactual recomposition.
Detailed analyses of these comparisons are provided in
Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Extended Experiments and Analyses ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
