<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">Position: quo vadis, unsupervised time series anomaly detection?</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_inbook">Proceedings of the 41st International Conference on Machine Learning</span>,
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_series">Proceedings of Machine Learning Research</span>, Vol. <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_volume">235</span>, <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_pages">pp. 43461–43476</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#A3.SS3.p1.1" title="C.3 Evaluation Metrics ‣ Appendix C Experimental Setup and Detailed Results ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§C.3</span></a>.
</span></li>
<li id="bib.bib36" class="ltx_bibitem ltx_bib_inproceedings"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_bib_key ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">[41]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_author">A. Huet, J. M. Navarro, and D. Rossi</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_year"> (2022)</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">Local evaluation of time series anomaly detection algorithms</span>.
</span>
