</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_pages">pp. 635–645</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#A3.I1.i3.p1.1" title="In C.3 Evaluation Metrics ‣ Appendix C Experimental Setup and Detailed Results ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3rd item</span></a>.
</span></li>
<li id="bib.bib37" class="ltx_bibitem ltx_bib_article"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_bib_key ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">[42]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_author">J. Paparrizos, P. Boniol, T. Palpanas, R. S. Tsay, A. J. Elmore, and M. J. Franklin</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_year"> (2022)</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">Volume under the surface: a new accuracy evaluation measure for time-series anomaly detection.</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_journal">Proc. VLDB Endow.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_volume">15</span> (<span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_number">11</span>), <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_pages">pp. 2774–2787</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#A3.I1.i4.p1.1" title="In C.3 Evaluation Metrics ‣ Appendix C Experimental Setup and Detailed Results ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4th item</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Details and Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides additional details for the theoretical analysis in the main text. We first formalize the limitation of predicting anomaly effects without temporal context, then prove Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Supervision-transfer risk). ‣ 4.4 Analysis of Supervision Transfer ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and finally clarify the regularity conditions, learning-error term, and scope of the resulting bound.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Contextual Realization Gap</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first elaborate on why transferable anomaly semantics alone are generally insufficient to determine their observable effects. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> denote temporal context, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> denote transferable anomaly information including semantic identity and support, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> denote the corresponding observation-level anomaly effect. Consider predictors <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> that predict the effect from transferable anomaly information without observing the temporal context.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming finite second moments, the conditional mean</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}(Z)=\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}(Z)=\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">minimizes the mean squared prediction error. By the conditional-variance decomposition,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{h}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{tr}\operatorname{Cov}(R\mid Z)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{h}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{tr}\operatorname{Cov}(R\mid Z)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In A.1 Contextual Realization Gap ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details and Proofs ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) characterizes the minimum squared error
of predicting the corresponding effect from <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> alone. In particular, when the same transferable anomaly information admits different conditional mean effects under different temporal contexts, context-independent prediction cannot fully recover the corresponding realized effect.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Allowing the predictor to additionally observe <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal predictor becomes</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f^{*}(C,Z)=\mathbb{E}[R\mid C,Z]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}(C,Z)=\mathbb{E}[R\mid C,Z],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">with minimum error</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{f}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-f(C,Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{tr}\operatorname{Cov}(R\mid C,Z)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{f}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-f(C,Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{tr}\operatorname{Cov}(R\mid C,Z)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The reduction in optimal squared error is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{h}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\inf_{f}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-f(C,Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{h}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-h(Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\inf_{f}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-f(C,Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left\|\mathbb{E}[R\mid C,Z]-\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left\|\mathbb{E}[R\mid C,Z]-\mathbb{E}[R\mid Z]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Hence, contextual conditioning improves the optimal squared-error prediction whenever temporal context changes the conditional mean realization of the same transferable anomaly information.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the deterministic idealization used for intuition in the main text, where</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=g(C,Z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=g(C,Z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">a predictor with access to both <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> can recover the corresponding effect exactly:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-g(C,Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|R-g(C,Z)\|_{2}^{2}\right]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">This motivates realizing sampled anomaly semantics conditionally on the target reference trajectory rather than treating semantic identity as a context-independent residual template.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This analysis concerns matched-effect prediction under squared loss. It does not establish a distributional lower bound for stochastic residual transfer or, by itself, imply an advantage in downstream anomaly detection.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Supervision-transfer risk). ‣ 4.4 Analysis of Supervision Transfer ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the target-reference distribution and let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=(r,m)\in\Xi" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=(r,m)\in\Xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">represent an anomaly-effect instance consisting of an observation-level residual <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and its temporal support <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. For a target reference <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{D}(x,\xi)=\ell\!\left(D(x+r),m\right),\qquad D\in\mathcal{H}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.247em;" width="0.247em"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{D}(x,\xi)=\ell\!\left(D(x+r),m\right),\qquad D\in\mathcal{H},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is the detector hypothesis class and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is the temporal detection loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ideal target-domain conditional distribution of anomaly effects and supports under reference <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional distribution induced by CAPS. We additionally introduce an analytical intermediate distribution
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which uses the same simulation-induced semantic prior and support sampling as CAPS but realizes them through an ideal target-context realization mechanism. Define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left[W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left[W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left[W_{1}\!\left(Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left[W_{1}\!\left(Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The first measures semantic-coverage and sampling mismatch relative to the ideal target effect distribution, while the second measures realization discrepancy relative to this ideal mechanism. This decomposition is analytical and depends on the chosen intermediate distribution <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}</annotation></semantics></math>; it is not intended as an identifiable decomposition of the two error sources from observed data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For any conditional effect distribution <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, define the matched training risk</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\nu}(D)=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left[\ell(D(x),\mathbf{0})+\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim\nu(\cdot\mid x)}\ell_{D}(x,\xi)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\nu}(D)=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left[\ell(D(x),\mathbf{0})+\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim\nu(\cdot\mid x)}\ell_{D}(x,\xi)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We write</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}=\mathcal{R}_{P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}},\qquad\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}=\mathcal{R}_{Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}=\mathcal{R}_{P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}},\qquad\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}=\mathcal{R}_{Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that, for <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the mapping</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\mapsto\ell_{D}(x,\xi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\mapsto\ell_{D}(x,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">is <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Xi,d_{\Xi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Xi,d_{\Xi})</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly over
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the nominal reference term
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(D(x),\mathbf{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(D(x),\mathbf{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is identical in the two risks,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left|\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)}\ell_{D}(x,\xi)-\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)}\ell_{D}(x,\xi)\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>tar</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}\left|\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)}\ell_{D}(x,\xi)-\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)}\ell_{D}(x,\xi)\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">By the Kantorovich–Rubinstein inequality,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L}{2}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the triangle inequality for <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+W_{1}\!\left(Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+W_{1}\!\left(Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Taking expectation over <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> therefore yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\leq\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P_{X}}W_{1}\!\left(P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x),Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\leq\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently,</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\left|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\right|\leq\frac{L}{2}\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\left|\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\right|\leq\frac{L}{2}\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and suppose that the learned detector <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Using Eq.( <a href="#A1.E26" title="In A.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details and Proofs ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(\hat{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(\hat{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})+\frac{L}{2}\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})+\frac{L}{2}\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}+\frac{L}{2}\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}+\frac{L}{2}\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)+L\Delta+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)+L\Delta+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(\hat{D})-\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\leq L\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}\right)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ideal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(\hat{D})-\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ideal}}(D)\leq L\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}\right)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.5" class="ltx_p">which proves Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Supervision-transfer risk). ‣ 4.4 Analysis of Supervision Transfer ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Additional Assumptions and Learning Error</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We finally clarify the regularity conditions and scope of the preceding analysis.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Wasserstein regularity.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The conditional distributions
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{tar}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi,*}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\Pi_{A}}^{\Xi}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>
are assumed to be measurable probability kernels with finite first moments under <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\Xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\Xi}</annotation></semantics></math>. We additionally assume that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and that the matched risks in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E22" title="In A.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details and Proofs ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) are finite. These conditions are sufficient for the Wasserstein quantities and expectations used in the proof to be well defined.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">A sufficient Lipschitz condition for binary cross-entropy.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposition requires the composed loss</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\mapsto\ell(D(x+r),m)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\mapsto\ell(D(x+r),m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">to admit a common Lipschitz constant uniformly over
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Binary cross-entropy is not globally Lipschitz when predicted probabilities approach <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. A sufficient condition is that, uniformly over <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, detector outputs on all relevant inputs satisfy</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(u)\in[\delta,1-\delta]^{T},\qquad 0&lt;\delta&lt;\frac{1}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(u)\in[\delta,1-\delta]^{T},\qquad 0&lt;\delta&lt;\frac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and that there exists a common constant <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{D}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{D}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{T}\|D(u)-D(v)\|_{1}\leq K_{D}\|u-v\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{T}\|D(u)-D(v)\|_{1}\leq K_{D}\|u-v\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">for all relevant inputs <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the averaged binary cross-entropy</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}(p,m)=-\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left[m_{t}\log p_{t}+(1-m_{t})\log(1-p_{t})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>BCE</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}(p,m)=-\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left[m_{t}\log p_{t}+(1-m_{t})\log(1-p_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">On <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}\in[\delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}\in[\delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math>, its variation with respect to prediction satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{\partial\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}}{\partial p_{t}}\right|\leq\frac{1}{T\delta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>BCE</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{\partial\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}}{\partial p_{t}}\right|\leq\frac{1}{T\delta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">while changing the binary label at a fixed prediction is bounded by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{T}\left|\log\frac{1-p_{t}}{p_{t}}\right|\leq\frac{1}{T}\log\frac{1-\delta}{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{T}\left|\log\frac{1-p_{t}}{p_{t}}\right|\leq\frac{1}{T}\log\frac{1-\delta}{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under the product metric</p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\Xi}\!\left((r,m),(r^{\prime},m^{\prime})\right)=\|r-r^{\prime}\|_{2}+\frac{1}{T}\|m-m^{\prime}\|_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\Xi}\!\left((r,m),(r^{\prime},m^{\prime})\right)=\|r-r^{\prime}\|_{2}+\frac{1}{T}\|m-m^{\prime}\|_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#A1.E30" title="In A sufficient Lipschitz condition for binary cross-entropy. ‣ A.3 Additional Assumptions and Learning Error ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details and Proofs ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) therefore implies</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}\!\left(D(x+r),m\right)-\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}\!\left(D(x+r^{\prime}),m^{\prime}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>BCE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>BCE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}\!\left(D(x+r),m\right)-\ell_{\mathrm{BCE}}\!\left(D(x+r^{\prime}),m^{\prime}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{K_{D}}{\delta}\|r-r^{\prime}\|_{2}+\log\frac{1-\delta}{\delta}\frac{1}{T}\|m-m^{\prime}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{K_{D}}{\delta}\|r-r^{\prime}\|_{2}+\log\frac{1-\delta}{\delta}\frac{1}{T}\|m-m^{\prime}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq L\,d_{\Xi}\!\left((r,m),(r^{\prime},m^{\prime})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq L\,d_{\Xi}\!\left((r,m),(r^{\prime},m^{\prime})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where one valid common constant is</p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\max\left\{\frac{K_{D}}{\delta},\log\frac{1-\delta}{\delta}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\max\left\{\frac{K_{D}}{\delta},\log\frac{1-\delta}{\delta}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">These conditions are only sufficient conditions for the theoretical bound; they need not be interpreted as additional constraints imposed by the CAPS training procedure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents ordinary detector-learning error under the CAPS-induced population risk rather than semantic-transfer discrepancy. To make this interpretation explicit, let
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the empirical risk on the recovered training set, and suppose that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{opt}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})\leq\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)+\epsilon_{\mathrm{opt}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})-\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(\hat{D})-\inf_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq 2\sup_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\left|\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)\right|+\epsilon_{\mathrm{opt}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>CAPS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq 2\sup_{D\in\mathcal{H}}\left|\widehat{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)-\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{CAPS}}(D)\right|+\epsilon_{\mathrm{opt}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the right-hand side of Eq. (<a href="#A1.E34" title="In Interpretation of ϵ_learn. ‣ A.3 Additional Assumptions and Learning Error ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details and Proofs ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>)
can be taken as <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}</annotation></semantics></math>, separating
finite-sample estimation error from optimization error.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This deterministic decomposition does not itself specify a finite-sample convergence rate. Establishing such a rate would additionally require assumptions accounting for temporal dependence and for dependence among generated counterparts constructed from shared references. Moreover, because Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Supervision-transfer risk). ‣ 4.4 Analysis of Supervision Transfer ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> compares detectors within the same hypothesis class <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, approximation error relative to an unrestricted Bayes-optimal detector is not included in <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>learn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{learn}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reference contamination.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bound compares ideal and CAPS matched-training risks under the same target-reference distribution and the same nominal reference label <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. It therefore isolates discrepancy associated with semantic coverage, sampling, and contextual realization. If a nominal target reference already contains an unobserved anomaly, assigning it the reference label <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> may introduce an additional supervision bias. Such contamination is not represented by
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> or
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>real</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{real}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is outside the scope of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Supervision-transfer risk). ‣ 4.4 Analysis of Supervision Transfer ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>; its empirical effect is examined separately in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Supervision Construction and Controlled Comparisons ‣ Appendix D Extended Experiments and Analyses ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Training and Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Overall Training and Inference Procedure</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ B.1 Overall Training and Inference Procedure ‣ Appendix B Training and Implementation Details ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the training, supervision-recovery,
and inference procedure of CAPS.
CAPS first learns structure and anomaly-semantic representations
from matched simulated normal–anomalous pairs using the objective
in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Structured Disentanglement for Transferable Anomaly Semantics ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
Within-pair counterfactual recomposition reconstructs each anomalous
sample from its anomaly-semantic code and its matched normal
reference’s structure code.
The representation modules are then fixed, mode-wise semantic priors
are estimated, and residual experts are trained.
During target-domain supervision recovery, sampled anomaly semantics
are conditionally realized on target references to construct matched
reference–counterpart pairs.
The detector is then trained with point-wise supervision on these
pairs and directly applied at inference.
In the standard setting, all modes are used without target anomaly
labels. With Diagnosis, limited known anomalies are used only to
select associated modes for targeted counterpart generation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Overall Training, Supervision Recovery, and Inference Procedure of CAPS</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Simulated correspondences
<math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{sim}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>sim</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{sim}}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{n},x_{a},m,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{n},x_{a},m,k)</annotation></semantics></math>,
unlabeled target training data
<math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{\mathrm{tr}}_{\mathrm{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi>tr</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{\mathrm{tr}}_{\mathrm{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
optional known anomalies <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
Diagnosis threshold <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> if enabled

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Semantic priors <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,
residual experts <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,
detector <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Paired representation learning</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each training batch sampled from <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{sim}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>sim</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{sim}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Encode simulated normal–anomalous pairs to obtain
<math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,s},z_{a,s},z_{n,a},z_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,s},z_{a,s},z_{n,a},z_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute the within-pair recomposition loss
<math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}=\mathrm{MSE}(\mathrm{Dec}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m),x_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cf</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Dec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}=\mathrm{MSE}(\mathrm{Dec}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m),x_{a})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              Update the encoder, representation heads, and auxiliary
decoders using
<math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{disen}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>disen</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>dis</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cf</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{disen}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            Freeze the trained encoder <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and representation heads
<math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{s},E_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{s},E_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mode organization and semantic-prior estimation</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            Establish mode assignments using the selected
knowledge-based or data-driven organization

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each mode <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              Encode anomaly samples assigned to mode <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and fit
the diagonal Gaussian
<math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}(z_{a})=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{k},\Sigma_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}(z_{a})=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{k},\Sigma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              Build the empirical mask pool <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
from correspondences assigned to mode <math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
            Form
<math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{A}(z_{a})=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{k}p_{k}(z_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{A}(z_{a})=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{k}p_{k}(z_{a})</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}=1/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}=1/K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Residual-expert training</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> Diagnosis is enabled <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
              Train the lightweight router on paired representations
<math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{n,s},z_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{n,s},z_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> using the established simulated mode assignments
to produce normalized mode-association scores

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each simulated training batch <span id="alg1.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute
<math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,s}=E_{s}(E(x_{n}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,s}=E_{s}(E(x_{n}))</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="alg1.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a}=E_{a}(E(x_{a}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a}=E_{a}(E(x_{a}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
              
              
              Form the observation-level effect <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=x_{a}-x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=x_{a}-x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
              
              
              Hard-route each sample according to its established
mode assignment <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
              
              
              Update the selected expert using
<math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>gen</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>
conditioned on <math id="alg1.l25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{n,s},z_{a},m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{n,s},z_{a},m)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l26.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mode selection for target generation</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> Diagnosis is enabled and <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l28.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
              
              
              Evaluate the router on
<math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{s}(E(x)),E_{a}(E(x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{s}(E(x)),E_{a}(E(x)))</annotation></semantics></math> for each
<math id="alg1.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}</annotation></semantics></math>
to obtain <math id="alg1.l29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute
<math id="alg1.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{q}_{k}\leftarrow\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}}q_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{q}_{k}\leftarrow\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}}q_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="alg1.l30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
              Sort modes such that
<math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{q}_{k_{(1)}}\geq\cdots\geq\bar{q}_{k_{(K)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{q}_{k_{(1)}}\geq\cdots\geq\bar{q}_{k_{(K)}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
              
              
              Set
<math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\rho}\leftarrow\min\left\{J:\sum_{j=1}^{J}\bar{q}_{k_{(j)}}\geq\rho\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\rho}\leftarrow\min\left\{J:\sum_{j=1}^{J}\bar{q}_{k_{(j)}}\geq\rho\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33:</span></span>
              
              
              Set
<math id="alg1.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\leftarrow\{k_{(1)},\ldots,k_{(J_{\rho})}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\leftarrow\{k_{(1)},\ldots,k_{(J_{\rho})}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l34.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">34:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l35.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">35:</span></span>
              
              
              Set <math id="alg1.l35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\leftarrow\{1,\ldots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\leftarrow\{1,\ldots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l36.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">36:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l36.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l36.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l37.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">37:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Target-domain supervision recovery</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l38" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l38.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">38:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize an empty pair list
<math id="alg1.l38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>tar</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l39" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l39.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">39:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each target reference
<math id="alg1.l39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}}\in\mathcal{D}^{\mathrm{tr}}_{\mathrm{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>tar</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>tar</mi><mi>tr</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}}\in\mathcal{D}^{\mathrm{tr}}_{\mathrm{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l39.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l40" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l40.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">40:</span></span>
              
              
              Extract
<math id="alg1.l40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i,s}^{\mathrm{tar}}=E_{s}(E(x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>tar</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>tar</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,s}^{\mathrm{tar}}=E_{s}(E(x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l41" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l41.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">41:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l41.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l41.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l42" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l42.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">42:</span></span>
              
              
               Sample
<math id="alg1.l42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}_{a}^{(k)}\sim p_{k}(z_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}_{a}^{(k)}\sim p_{k}(z_{a})</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="alg1.l42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\sim\mathcal{M}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\sim\mathcal{M}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l43" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l43.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">43:</span></span>
              
              
               Generate
<math id="alg1.l43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="alg1.l43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on
<math id="alg1.l43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{i,s}^{\mathrm{tar}},\tilde{z}_{a}^{(k)},m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>tar</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{i,s}^{\mathrm{tar}},\tilde{z}_{a}^{(k)},m)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l44" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l44.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">44:</span></span>
              
              
               Construct
<math id="alg1.l44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{i,a}^{(k)}=x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}}+\hat{r}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>tar</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{i,a}^{(k)}=x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}}+\hat{r}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l45" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l45.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">45:</span></span>
              
              
               Append
<math id="alg1.l45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big((x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}},\mathbf{0}),(\hat{x}_{i,a}^{(k)},m)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>tar</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big((x_{i}^{\mathrm{tar}},\mathbf{0}),(\hat{x}_{i,a}^{(k)},m)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
to <math id="alg1.l45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>tar</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l46" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l46.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">46:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l46.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l46.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l47" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l47.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">47:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l47.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l47.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l48" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l48.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">48:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l48.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detector training</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l49" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l49.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">49:</span></span>
              
              
            Train
<math id="alg1.l49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{T}\rightarrow[0,1]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{T}\rightarrow[0,1]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>
on <math id="alg1.l49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>tar</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{P}}_{\mathrm{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math>
using averaged point-wise BCE with equal weight on the
reference and generated branches

</div>
<div id="alg1.l50" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l50.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">50:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l50.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test-time scoring:</span> Output <math id="alg1.l50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for each test sequence <math id="alg1.l50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Paired Representation Learning and Counterfactual Recomposition</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Representation learning uses simulated correspondences
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{n},x_{a},m,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{n},x_{a},m,k)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normal reference,
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is its matched anomalous counterpart, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> specifies the
anomaly support, and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a coarse simulated anomaly family.
Each pair shares a temporal reference while exposing an
anomaly-induced change. The family label <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> provides the default
organization for subsequent prior estimation and expert training,
while the representation-learning objective operates on the
matched observations and their support.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Structured Disentanglement for Transferable Anomaly Semantics ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the shared encoder and
two representation heads produce <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a,s}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,a}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The reconstruction and background objectives constrain the
representations to explain the observations and preserve their
shared temporal background. The disentanglement objective
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>dis</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}</annotation></semantics></math> encourages agreement between
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a,s}</annotation></semantics></math>, while suppressing anomaly-semantic
activation <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,a}</annotation></semantics></math> for the normal reference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Within-pair counterfactual recomposition further constrains how
the learned factors are used. The ordinary anomalous reconstruction
uses the structure code <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a,s}</annotation></semantics></math> extracted from <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For recomposition, we replace this code with <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,s}</annotation></semantics></math> from its
matched normal reference, while retaining <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Dec}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m)=\mathrm{base}(z_{n,s})+\mathrm{res}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Dec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>base</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>res</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Dec}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m)=\mathrm{base}(z_{n,s})+\mathrm{res}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The reconstruction target remains the same matched anomalous
observation <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}=\mathrm{MSE}\bigl(\mathrm{Dec}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m),x_{a}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cf</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Dec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}=\mathrm{MSE}\bigl(\mathrm{Dec}(z_{n,s},z_{a},m),x_{a}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Both representations originate from the same simulated pair.
This constraint encourages anomaly information to remain usable
with structure extracted from a normal observation.
The residual decoder is conditioned on both factors, allowing
the reconstructed effect to depend on the reference context.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The complete representation-learning objective is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{disen}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>disen</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>dis</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cf</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{disen}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">All four terms are evaluated on matched-pair minibatches, and the
encoder, representation heads, and auxiliary decoders are optimized
jointly. After representation learning, the encoder and heads are
fixed for semantic-prior estimation and residual-expert training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Semantic Prior, Mode Organization, and Diagnosis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After paired representation learning, the encoder and representation
heads are fixed, yielding a shared continuous anomaly-semantic
space <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. The mode index <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> provides a coarse
organization of heterogeneous simulated anomaly semantics within
this common space; it does not define separate latent spaces or
an exhaustive taxonomy of target-domain anomalies.
Continuous semantic variation is retained within each mode through
<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, while mode organization provides a coarse specialization
structure for prior estimation and context-conditioned realization.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mode organization.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider two strategies for organizing the learned
anomaly-semantic space. The default strategy is
<em id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">knowledge-based</em>. Based on the temporal characteristics of
the simulated anomaly operations, we organize them into three
coarse modes,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K=3:\qquad\text{trend},\quad\text{periodic},\quad\text{point}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mtext>trend</mtext><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>periodic</mtext><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>point</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3:\qquad\text{trend},\quad\text{periodic},\quad\text{point}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3</annotation></semantics></math> follows from this source-side organization rather
than being selected through target-domain supervision or
latent-space clustering. Each mode still contains continuous
variation in its operation-specific configuration parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As an alternative, we consider a fully <em id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">data-driven</em>
organization that does not use the predefined
trend–periodic–point assignments. After representation learning,
the frozen anomaly-semantic codes <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> are organized directly
in <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. We evaluate</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{1,3,5,7\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{1,3,5,7\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> treats the semantic space as a single mode and
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> uses <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-means clustering to obtain the corresponding
mode assignments. These assignments replace the simulator-defined
mode labels throughout subsequent prior estimation and expert
specialization. For the clustering-based variants, the same
assignments also define the mode-specific mask pools and, when
applicable, the supervision labels for the Diagnosis router.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The two strategies therefore examine different sources of semantic
organization: the knowledge-based construction introduces a coarse
inductive bias derived from temporal anomaly structure, whereas
the data-driven construction derives the organization directly
from the learned semantic representations.
As evaluated in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Semantic Coverage and Mode Organization ‣ Appendix D Extended Experiments and Analyses ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, the
knowledge-based three-mode organization achieves the strongest
overall performance and is therefore adopted as the default setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Changing <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in the data-driven variants changes not only the
specialization granularity but, under our default generation
protocol, also the total number of residual experts and the number
of generated counterparts per target reference. Comparisons across
different values of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> should therefore be interpreted as
end-to-end mode-organization configurations rather than as an
isolated measure of specialization granularity.
In contrast, the knowledge-based and data-driven configurations
with <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3</annotation></semantics></math> use the same number of modes and provide a more direct
comparison of the two organization strategies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mode-wise semantic prior.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given mode organization, let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{k}=\left\{z_{a}^{(j)}:k_{j}=k\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{k}=\left\{z_{a}^{(j)}:k_{j}=k\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">denote the anomaly-semantic codes assigned to mode <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
We estimate a diagonal Gaussian</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}(z_{a})=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{k},\Sigma_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}(z_{a})=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{k},\Sigma_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{k}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Z}_{k}|}\sum_{z\in\mathcal{Z}_{k}}z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Z}_{k}|}\sum_{z\in\mathcal{Z}_{k}}z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the diagonal empirical covariance of the
corresponding semantic codes. The resulting simulation-induced
semantic prior is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{A}(z_{a})=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{k}p_{k}(z_{a}),\qquad\pi_{k}=\frac{1}{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{A}(z_{a})=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{k}p_{k}(z_{a}),\qquad\pi_{k}=\frac{1}{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The Gaussian components provide a coarse multimodal approximation
within the same continuous semantic space rather than defining
independent anomaly spaces. Under the standard generation
procedure, each target reference receives one generated counterpart
from each mode, consistent with the uniform mixture weights.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Expert specialization.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During simulated-domain expert training, each sample is hard-routed
according to its established mode assignment <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the knowledge-based organization, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the
simulated anomaly family; under the data-driven organization,
it is determined by the semantic-space clustering.
The corresponding residual expert <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimized only with
samples assigned to that mode.
Such coarse specialization is intended to reduce interference
among heterogeneous semantic regions during context-conditioned
realization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The lightweight router used for Diagnosis neither determines the
mode organization nor serves as the training gate for the residual
experts. Mode assignments are established before expert training,
whereas the router is used only to associate limited known target
anomalies with the already constructed modes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diagnosis with limited known anomalies.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The standard CAPS setting requires no target-domain anomaly labels
and uses all available modes,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}=\{1,\ldots,K\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}=\{1,\ldots,K\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When limited known target anomalies are available, CAPS(Diagnosis)
uses a lightweight router to estimate their associations with
the simulation-derived modes. During simulated training, the router
takes <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{n,s},z_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{n,s},z_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> from matched correspondences and is
supervised by their established mode assignments.
For a known target anomaly <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, its input is
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{s}(E(x)),E_{a}(E(x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{s}(E(x)),E_{a}(E(x)))</annotation></semantics></math>, so no matched normal counterpart is
required. It outputs normalized mode-association scores</p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x)\geq 0,\qquad\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x)\geq 0,\qquad\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Given a small known-anomaly set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we compute</p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{q}_{k}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}}q_{k}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>known</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{q}_{k}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{known}}}q_{k}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{q}_{k_{(1)}}\geq\bar{q}_{k_{(2)}}\geq\cdots\geq\bar{q}_{k_{(K)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{q}_{k_{(1)}}\geq\bar{q}_{k_{(2)}}\geq\cdots\geq\bar{q}_{k_{(K)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">denote the sorted associations.
We use a cumulative-association threshold</p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">and define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\rho}=\min\left\{J:\sum_{j=1}^{J}\bar{q}_{k_{(j)}}\geq\rho\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\rho}=\min\left\{J:\sum_{j=1}^{J}\bar{q}_{k_{(j)}}\geq\rho\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">with the retained mode set</p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\rho}=\left\{k_{(1)},\ldots,k_{(J_{\rho})}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\rho}=\left\{k_{(1)},\ldots,k_{(J_{\rho})}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The selected modes are used equally for counterpart generation,
corresponding to</p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{A,\mathcal{K}_{\rho}}(z_{a})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{K}_{\rho}|}\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{\rho}}p_{k}(z_{a})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{A,\mathcal{K}_{\rho}}(z_{a})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{K}_{\rho}|}\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{\rho}}p_{k}(z_{a}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The known anomalies are used only for mode association and targeted
counterpart generation rather than as detector-training labels.
The router is unnecessary in the standard CAPS setting and is not
used by the final detector at inference.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Architecture and Optimization Details</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Two-stage representation and generation training. ‣ B.4 Architecture and Optimization Details ‣ Appendix B Training and Implementation Details ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes the main architectural
and optimization configurations used in CAPS.
Unless otherwise specified, all reported results use an input
length of 256 and the knowledge-based three-mode organization
described in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Semantic Prior, Mode Organization, and Diagnosis ‣ Appendix B Training and Implementation Details ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.
The representation and generation modules are trained in two stages.
We first optimize the paired representation-learning objective
and then freeze the encoder and representation heads.
The fixed representations are subsequently used to estimate the
semantic priors and train the hard-routed residual experts.
The detector is trained independently on the recovered
target-domain reference–counterpart pairs.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Two-stage representation and generation training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the first stage, the shared encoder <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, structure head <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>,
anomaly-semantic head <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, and auxiliary decoders are jointly
optimized on minibatches of matched simulated normal–anomalous
pairs using</p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{disen}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>disen</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>dis</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>cf</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{disen}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{rec}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{base}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dis}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{cf}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We use Adam with a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, a batch size
of 32, and train the representation modules for 60 epochs.
After this stage, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> are frozen,
thereby fixing the learned structure and anomaly-semantic spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the second stage, the frozen representation modules are used
to extract <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n,s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> from the simulated
correspondences. The mode-wise diagonal Gaussian priors
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are estimated from these fixed semantic
codes, and the residual experts are optimized using
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>gen</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each simulated sample is hard-routed according to its established
mode assignment.
The residual-generation stage is trained for 100 epochs using
Adam with the same learning rate and batch size.
We use a diffusion horizon of 200 steps and run the full
200-step reverse process for counterpart generation.
The lightweight router is trained only when CAPS(Diagnosis)
is evaluated and does not participate in standard expert routing.
The base and residual decoders in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Two-stage representation and generation training. ‣ B.4 Architecture and Optimization Details ‣ Appendix B Training and Implementation Details ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
are auxiliary reconstruction modules used during representation
learning.
The diffusion experts operate directly in observation-level
residual space; the clean-residual estimate defined in
Sec. <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Context-Conditioned Anomaly-Effect Generation ‣ 4 Context-Anchored Pair Supervision ‣ Supervision Recovery for Time Series Anomaly Detection via Context-Anchored Pairing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> is used to evaluate
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> during training, whereas
counterpart generation uses the full reverse diffusion process.</p>
</div>
